INT. ABANDONED SUBWAY PLATFORM - NIGHT

Tiled walls. Dripping pipes. A flickering clock reads 3:07.

INSPECTOR LUCIEN MARCH, 50s, in a trench coat, waits with his hands in his pockets. Across the tracks, VESPER DUNNE, 30s, in red heels, holds a small case. Between them stands a HOODED MAN, 40s, and a BOY, 12, who sells newspapers at the exit.

LUCIEN
Miss Dunne. Punctual.

VESPER
Inspector March. You came alone.

LUCIEN
I always do.

The Boy waves a paper. The Hooded Man steps behind a pillar. Lucien sees it.

LUCIEN (CONT'D)
Who's your friend?

VESPER
Nobody. Just the usual.

LUCIEN
The usual doesn't wear a gun.

Vesper smiles. Tosses the case across the tracks. Lucien catches it. The Hooded Man draws. Lucien drops the case and ducks. The Boy shrieks and bolts. Vesper kicks the Hooded Man's knee. He cries out. They struggle and tumble. Lucien tackles them both.

LUCIEN (CONT'D)
Vesper!

VESPER
Stop calling me that!

The gun skitters along the tile. A train horn blares in the tunnel. Everyone freezes. Light blooms from the dark. Vesper snatches the case. The Hooded Man grabs her ankle.

HOODED MAN
Where's the money, Vesper?

VESPER
Wouldn't you like to know.

The train roars in. Lucien shoves them both flat as the cars thunder past. Wind whips coats. When the last car clears, the platform is empty. The case lies open, filled with newspaper clippings.
